<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka T-bill yields continue to ease.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka T-bill yields continue to ease.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yields of three, six and 12-month treasury bills fell by 0.06, 0.28 and 0.34 percentage points respectively at Wednesday's auction, the Central Bank said, adding its purchases amounted to 663 million rupees.</p>
<p>		   Bids received   Bids accepted   Avg yield</p>
<p>    3 months     1,392	     1,011	  12.66 (12.72)</p>
<p>    6 months     1,927		 900	  13.87 (14.15)</p>
<p>    12 months    1,257		 850	  14.23 (14.57)</p>
<p>    Total	  4,576	     2,761</p>
<p>NOTE - Bids in million rupees, yields in percent (previous week's yields in brackets). --Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
